window: vmlab: every key goes to macOS while the window has the keyboard; the pointer is free

One rule for the keyboard and the pointer, the same as the Windows window's:
  - the keyboard is captured from the moment the window gains it until it loses it (upstream:
    from a click into the picture), the desktop's own shortcuts included (Super is Command);
  - the pointer is never held in the picture (upstream confines it), so the title bar and
    the rest of the desktop stay one move away;
  - no release chord (upstream: Ctrl+Alt+Super): another window takes the keyboard with a
    click, and GNOME's own Super+Escape gives the desktop its shortcuts back;
  - the click that gives the window the keyboard is sent to macOS (upstream: swallowed).

Applies after window-full-screen-clipboard-file-drop.dev.patch.
